  + Split every butterfly cluster into four real members — DSP modular multiplier, symmetric modular adder, symmetric modular subtractor, and a pipeline register — modeled 4x with distinct ids
  + Added the Conflict-Free Schedule/FSM Controller (the loop-reordering contribution) on the right cluster
  + Raised component heights and tightened the connection graph into a clean assembly order rooted at the PCB
  · gap: Add an exploded copy of one butterfly cluster floating ~2.5 m above the board to make the radix-4 datapath unmistakable from ISO
  · gap: Add an FPGA die/package outline plus a heatsink so the silhouette reads instantly as an FPGA accelerator, not a generic PCB
  · gap: Differentiate a forward-NTT vs inverse-NTT (INTT) annotation/path and vary primitives further (e.g. capsule pipeline FIFOs) for the geometry axis

